From 5db15ccdb96281d7204aeaae0374fe0a80737f89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:24:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] server: keep eagle3 cache boundary across F4
 partial-reject resets

The F4 reset cleared the whole eagle3 impl state (set_state empty), including
the boundary row get_state must serve to prompt_save/create_checkpoint. When a
task's final verify round is a partial reject, the state stays empty through
idle and the next prompt_save skips ('required speculative state unavailable'):
with the history only in the slot, a cold fallback then destroys it (run7
03/09: 5 skipped saves, 3 full re-prefills 82k/87k/114k).

Split the state: pending_*/verify_* stay the draft-sync pair cleared by the F4
reset (drafting behavior byte-identical); boundary_* mirrors the accepted row
and survives it. get_state reads boundary_*. New draft_sync_reset primitive
defaults to the old set_state({}) for every other impl (dflash unchanged).
Blob format unchanged: existing disk entries stay restorable.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
